\title{One order for UBI's order engine: an order template and the synthetic type that works it}
\description{
A synthetic order is one ordinary order body, the template, plus a \code{synthetic} object naming the type and holding that type's own settings. UBI's order engine then places, watches, changes and cancels the real orders the type is made of. \code{SyntheticOrder} holds the template and sends it through \code{TradeableInstrument$place_order()}; each subclass, such as \code{BracketOrder}, adds its own settings.

The template is validated by UBI exactly as a plain order is, and most types use it for every real order they send, changing only what they must. Nothing is checked here before sending.
}
