\subsection{\code{SyntheticOrder$place()}}{
  Sends the order to UBI's order engine through \code{TradeableInstrument$place_order()}, and keeps the \code{parent_id} the engine answers with.
  \subsection{Usage}{
    \if{html}{\out{<div class="r">}}
    \preformatted{SyntheticOrder$place()}
    \if{html}{\out{</div>}}
  }
  \subsection{Details}{
    Errors: signals \code{BadRequestError} when a template field is invalid, or one of this type's own settings is missing or wrong; \code{LossLockoutError} when the day's loss is past UBI's daily loss limit; \code{ConflictError} when the engine refused to act on the account's state, such as a post-only order that would cross the book or a reduce-only leg that would not reduce the position, or the engine had already started this order before a restart; \code{RateLimitError} when the broker's daily order cap has no room for this order; \code{ServiceUnavailableError} when no broker could take the order, a price UBI needed could not be read, or the order engine is not running; \code{OrderOutcomeUnknownError} when the engine did not answer in time, so the order may still be placed; and another \code{UnifiedBrokerInterfaceError} subclass for any other failure reported by, or on the way to, UBI.
  }
  \subsection{Returns}{
    The named list \code{place_order()} returns. A type that acts at once answers with the broker's answer and a \code{parent_id}; a type that waits for a price or a time, or whose limit orders UBI holds until the market reaches them, answers with an \code{outcome} of \code{armed}, a \code{broker} and \code{order_id} of \code{NULL}, and a \code{parent_id}, which is the only handle on the order until it reaches a broker. The types that send several orders at once, \code{freeze_slicer}, \code{ladder}, \code{grid}, \code{two_sided_quote}, \code{basket}, \code{oco}, \code{bracket} and \code{two_sided_breakout}, answer with a \code{legs} list, one entry per order with its plan \code{path}, \code{instrument_id}, \code{outcome}, \code{order_id} and \code{status_message}, and one combined \code{outcome}: \code{accepted} when every order was accepted, \code{partial} with HTTP 207 when only some were, which is returned rather than signalled, and otherwise \code{unknown} or \code{rejected}, which are signalled.
  }
