\subsection{\code{SyntheticOrder$cancel()}}{
  Cancels this order in UBI's order engine, with every leg it still has resting at a broker.

A position the order has already opened is not closed.
  \subsection{Usage}{
    \if{html}{\out{<div class="r">}}
    \preformatted{SyntheticOrder$cancel()}
    \if{html}{\out{</div>}}
  }
  \subsection{Details}{
    Errors: signals \code{ValueError} when the order has not been placed, so there is no parent to cancel; \code{NotFoundError} when the engine holds no parent with this id; \code{ConflictError} when the parent has already finished; and another \code{UnifiedBrokerInterfaceError} subclass for any other failure reported by, or on the way to, UBI.
  }
  \subsection{Returns}{
    The named list \code{TradeableInstrument$cancel_parent()} returns, with \code{parent_id}, \code{synthetic_type}, \code{state} and a \code{cancelled_legs} list. Its \code{state} is \code{cancelling} rather than \code{cancelled} when a broker refused a leg's cancel, so that leg may still be live.
  }
  \subsection{Examples}{
    \if{html}{\out{<div class="r example copy">}}
